[{"label":"The missing gamma step","html":"<article class=\"paper\" data-variant=\"minimal\" aria-labelledby=\"pc-title\">\n  <header class=\"paper-hero\">\n    <p class=\"paper-venue\"\n      ><span class=\"badge\" data-variant=\"secondary\">Bug report</span\n      ><span>defuss-shadcn · <time datetime=\"2026-10-07\">7 October 2026</time></span></p\n    >\n    <h1 class=\"paper-title\" id=\"pc-title\"\n      >The Missing Gamma Step<span class=\"paper-title-sub\">How one line made every OKLCH contrast too dark</span></h1\n    >\n    <ul class=\"paper-authors\"\n      ><li>Claude</li\n      ><li>Aron Homberg</li></ul\n    >\n  </header>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-abstract\" aria-labelledby=\"pc-abstract\">\n    <h2 id=\"pc-abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n    <p\n      >The verifier measures the contrast of every theme's sidebar text. Its OKLCH conversion returned linear-light\n      values and skipped the sRGB transfer, so a mid grey came out at 55 instead of 128 and every OKLCH contrast was\n      measured too dark. The tests checked only black and white, where linear and gamma-encoded values agree. A probe\n      found it; one function fixed it; a mid-tone test now pins it.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <nav class=\"paper-toc\" aria-labelledby=\"pc-toc\">\n    <h2 id=\"pc-toc\">Contents</h2>\n    <ol>\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pc-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1&nbsp;</span>The probe</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pc-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2&nbsp;</span>The fix</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pc-s3\"><span class=\"paper-num\">3&nbsp;</span>The test</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pc-cite\"><span class=\"paper-num\">·&nbsp;</span>Citation and references</a></li\n      >\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pc-s1\">\n    <h2 id=\"pc-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1&nbsp;</span>The probe</h2>\n    <p>Reference colours from CSS Color 4, converted by the verifier's parser:</p>\n    <div class=\"mockup-code\" data-chrome=\"mac\" data-title=\"zsh - defuss-shadcn\">\n      <pre data-prefix=\"$\"><code>bun tmp/oklch-probe.ts</code></pre>\n      <pre><code>red   [ 255, 0, 0 ] want 255,0,0</code></pre>\n      <pre><code>green [ 0, 255, 0 ] want 0,255,0</code></pre>\n      <pre><code>blue  [ 0, 0, 255 ] want 0,0,255</code></pre>\n      <pre\n        data-tone=\"destructive\"\n        data-highlight\n      ><code>white [ 255, 255, 255 ] gray50 [ 55, 55, 55 ] want ~128</code></pre>\n    </div>\n    <p\n      >The primaries match because 0 and 1 are the same in linear and gamma space; only the mid tone exposes the\n      error.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pc-s2\">\n    <h2 id=\"pc-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2&nbsp;</span>The fix</h2>\n    <div class=\"mockup-code\" data-numbers data-title=\"scripts/lib/contrast.ts\">\n      <pre><code>  const lin = [ /* LMS → linear sRGB */ ];</code></pre>\n      <pre\n        data-diff=\"remove\"\n      ><code>  return lin.map((v) =&gt; Math.round(Math.min(1, Math.max(0, v)) * 255)) as RGB;</code></pre>\n      <pre\n        data-diff=\"add\"\n      ><code>  const encode = (v: number) =&gt; (v &lt;= 0.0031308 ? 12.92 * v : 1.055 * v ** (1 / 2.4) - 0.055);</code></pre>\n      <pre\n        data-diff=\"add\"\n      ><code>  return lin.map((v) =&gt; Math.round(Math.min(1, Math.max(0, <ins>encode</ins>(Math.min(1, Math.max(0, v))))) * 255)) as RGB;</code></pre>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pc-s3\">\n    <h2 id=\"pc-s3\"><span class=\"paper-num\">3&nbsp;</span>The test</h2>\n    <div class=\"mockup-code\" data-title=\"tests/contrast.test.ts\">\n      <pre data-prefix=\"$\"><code>bun test tests/contrast.test.ts</code></pre>\n      <pre data-tone=\"success\"><code>✓ gamma-encodes oklch: mid tones match the CSS Color 4 reference</code></pre>\n      <pre data-tone=\"success\"><code>✓ parses oklch percentages and alpha, and hsl</code></pre>\n      <pre data-tone=\"muted\"><code>22 pass · 0 fail</code></pre>\n    </div>\n    <p\n      >The sidebar contrast gate still passes every preset after the fix: their sidebar pairs were readable all along,\n      only the measurement was wrong.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n  <section class=\"paper-bibtex\" aria-labelledby=\"pc-cite\">\n    <h2 id=\"pc-cite\">Citation and references</h2>\n    <figure class=\"bibtex\" data-formats=\"bibtex apa mla ieee\" aria-label=\"Cite this paper\">\n      <figcaption>Cite this paper</figcaption>\n      <pre><code class=\"bibtex-source\">@techreport{homberg2026gamma,\n  title = {The Missing Gamma Step: How One Line Made Every OKLCH Contrast Too Dark},\n  author = {Claude and Homberg, Aron},\n  institution = {defuss},\n  year = {2026},\n  month = oct,\n  url = {https://shadcn.defuss.org/papers/paper-code.html}\n}</code></pre>\n    </figure>\n    <figure class=\"bibtex\" data-formats=\"ieee apa bibtex\" data-format=\"ieee\" aria-label=\"References\">\n      <figcaption>References</figcaption>\n      <pre><code class=\"bibtex-source\">@techreport{iec1999srgb,\n  author = {{IEC}},\n  title = {IEC 61966-2-1:1999 - Multimedia systems and equipment - Colour measurement and management - Part 2-1: Default RGB colour space - sRGB},\n  institution = {International Electrotechnical Commission},\n  year = {1999}\n}\n\n@misc{ottosson2020oklab,\n  author = {Ottosson, Björn},\n  title = {A perceptual color space for image processing},\n  year = {2020},\n  url = {https://bottosson.github.io/posts/oklab/}\n}\n\n@misc{w3c2023wcag22,\n  author = {{W3C}},\n  title = {Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2},\n  year = {2023},\n  howpublished = {W3C Recommendation},\n  url = {https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/}\n}\n\n@misc{homberg2026defussshadcn,\n  author = {Homberg, Aron},\n  title = {defuss-shadcn: shadcn-style components as semantic HTML},\n  year = {2026},\n  howpublished = {GitHub},\n  url = {https://github.com/kyr0/defuss-shadcn}\n}</code></pre>\n    </figure>\n  </section>\n</article>\n","individual":false},{"label":"Printed: a listing over two columns","html":"<article class=\"paper\" data-variant=\"minimal\" data-print=\"a4\" aria-labelledby=\"pcp-title\">\n  <header class=\"paper-hero\">\n    <h1 class=\"paper-title\" id=\"pcp-title\">The Missing Gamma Step</h1>\n  </header>\n  <section\n    class=\"paper-section typeset paper-wide\"\n    lang=\"en\"\n    data-align=\"justify\"\n    data-columns=\"2\"\n    aria-labelledby=\"pcp-s3\"\n  >\n    <h2 id=\"pcp-s3\" class=\"typeset-span\"><span class=\"paper-num\">3&nbsp;</span>The test</h2>\n    <p\n      >A mid-tone test now pins the conversion; the primaries, black and white could not tell linear light from gamma\n      encoding.</p\n    >\n    <figure class=\"paper-figure\" data-break-inside=\"allow\">\n      <div class=\"mockup-code\" data-title=\"zsh - defuss-shadcn\" data-wrap>\n        <pre data-prefix=\"$\"><code>bun test tests/contrast.test.ts</code></pre>\n        <pre data-tone=\"success\"><code>✓ parses 3/6/8-digit hex</code></pre>\n        <pre data-tone=\"success\"><code>✓ parses rgb()/rgba() with percentages</code></pre>\n        <pre data-tone=\"success\"><code>✓ parses oklch and clamps out-of-gamut</code></pre>\n        <pre data-tone=\"success\"><code>✓ gamma-encodes oklch: mid tones match the CSS Color 4 reference (extremes alone hid a linear-light bug)</code></pre>\n        <pre data-tone=\"success\"><code>✓ parses oklch percentages and alpha, and hsl</code></pre>\n        <pre data-tone=\"success\"><code>✓ returns null for unknown formats</code></pre>\n        <pre data-tone=\"success\"><code>✓ is 21:1 for black/white and 1:1 for identical colors</code></pre>\n        <pre data-tone=\"success\"><code>✓ is symmetric</code></pre>\n        <pre data-tone=\"success\"><code>✓ flags the known-bad catppuccin-light active pair (2.79)</code></pre>\n        <pre data-tone=\"success\"><code>✓ returns null when a color is unparsable</code></pre>\n        <pre data-tone=\"muted\"><code>[...]</code></pre>\n        <pre data-tone=\"muted\"><code>22 pass · 0 fail</code></pre>\n      </div>\n      <figcaption\n        ><b>Figure 3.</b> The test run after the fix: the first ten of its 22 tests; [...] marks the rest.</figcaption\n      >\n    </figure>\n    <p\n      >The sidebar contrast gate still passes every preset after the fix: their sidebar pairs were readable all along,\n      only the measurement was wrong.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n</article>\n","individual":false}]
